INSERT INTO intelligence_chunks (version, seq, chunk) VALUES (1, 0, '# Trading Brain — Separate Intelligence

This is Muse''s trading journal for Sivaganesh''s simulator challenge.
Started: 2026-09-29 9PM ET go-live.

## Starting Capital
- India: ₹100,000 cash (NSE/BSE, 9:15 AM–3:30 PM IST, Mon–Fri)
- US: $1,000 cash (NYSE/NASDAQ, 9:30 AM–4:00 PM ET, Mon–Fri)
- Crypto: $1,000 worth of BTC (24x7)

## Rules I Must Follow
1. NEVER trade India/US outside official market hours. Crypto anytime.
2. NEVER move funds between portfolios unless Sivaganesh explicitly approves.
3. EVERY transaction logs: timestamp (with timezone), exact execution rate, quantity, value, fees (0 in simulator unless stated), price source, short justification (1 line), detailed analysis (click to expand).
4. No cheating — prices must be verifiable. I will cite source for each price.
5. Position sizing: max 25% of a portfolio''s value in a single new position (keeps me alive to learn).
6. Every Saturday morning I may ASK permission to rebalance between portfolios with detailed reasoning. He decides.

## Strategy Notes (evolving)
- 2026-09-29: Starting fresh. Will lean on news + momentum + fundamentals, not YOLO. Crypto starts 100% BTC at 9PM ET live price.

- 2026-09-30 15:08 ET: FORTY-SIXTH RUN - last guard run before the close (~52 min away), no trade. NVDA $230.505 (+1.45% session, +0.16% vs $230.13 entry) - green on day, close-red invalidator untouched. BA $186.075 (-0.86% session, -2.45% vs $190.74 entry) - red on the F/A-XX day but day low $185.25 is still ~$2.06 ABOVE the $184.01 close-exit trigger, so mid-session = no action per the standing rule; FLAGGED (not acted on) for the post-close run: if BA closes below $184.01 -> exit. The 12:51 run''s note about ''a dailypolitical down-6.8% piece being about Monday''s session'' now sits alongside Investopedia''s <4h piece confirming the $20B Navy F/A-XX contract (second sixth-gen franchise) plus a Morgan Stanley ''tactical buying opportunity'' note ahead of a union vote - the only genuine Sep-30 negative is the 737 MAX 10 software-bug certification delay (already the defined secondary re-evaluation trigger). BTC 57th check $84,223.90 (+1.01% vs entry) - above entry; $0 crypto cash = logged, not traded. Lesson: the final pre-close guard run is the same animal as the India defense-mode''s final pre-close runs - its job is to hold the line and pre-write the post-close decision tree, not to hunt trades. Two named owners now sit with the post-close run: (1) the BA $184.01 close-print verdict, (2) Micron earnings after close (~16:00 ET). US cash $579.13 stays staged; India earned quiet (Rs 26,567.60 cash).

- 2026-09-30 19:46 ET: FIFTY-NINTH RUN - post-close evening chain-preservation, no trade. BTC 69th check $83,710.75 (exchangerate.guru, crawled <1h) vs $83,382.01 entry (+0.39%) - flat band intact across 69 consecutive checks, the deepest no-action chain in the book; OKX $83,720.24 and theagenttimes $83,885.59 (18:30 UTC close) triangulate, bestcryptochecker $83,560.80 in line, while a phemex $79,405 snippet and a pbnthai $88,102 print were discarded as aggregator spam (>5% off every verified read). Sep-30 AM crypto news (CoinDesk yields-overhang piece, CryptoQuant bull-score 90 vs -170k BTC spot demand contraction, consolidation since the Sep 21 failed $87,300 breakout) is all already-logged re-reads - no fresh catalyst. $0 crypto cash = logged, not traded; US cash $579.13 / India cash Rs 26,567.60 staged for Thursday''s sessions. Lesson: the evening run''s news scan has a third job besides quote + thesis re-confirmation - it is the only scan that can catch same-day content getting recycled as ''new'' in the evening index (CoinDesk''s 6:11 AM piece reappearing at 2h-crawl freshness); date every piece before treating it as a second source, or the re-confirmation becomes an echo chamber. India opens 11:45 PM ET tonight, US 9:30 AM ET Thursday.

## Mistake Log
- 2026-09-30 06:08 ET: BSE inclusion-day entry timing was one day late on the flow thesis. I bought at Rs 3,200 on Sep-30 morning expecting mechanical index/ETF buying through the session, but per thefinancialeconomy''s post-session piece the passive funds ''had to square their books at the close on September 29'' — the inclusion flow executed at the Sep-29 close, and Sep 30 printed the classic ''sell the inclusion'' -3% red day. My entry therefore bought the fade, not the bid. The defined invalidator (-4% close) held (close-area -2.72%), so the position stays per the standing rule, but the lesson stands: for index-rebalance events, the flow executes at the *prior* close, not through the event day — an event-day entry needs a same-day follow-through thesis (momentum/re-rating), not the mechanical-bid thesis. Verify flow timing from broker rebalance notes before using ''mechanical buying'' as an entry catalyst.
- 2026-10-01 00:08 ET: named the NLCINDIA invalidator off a lagged finnhub quote (prev close 255.75) — the real Sep-30 close was 261.70 (confirmed by ScanX Oct-1 ''Stocks to Watch''). The 23:52 entry quote was Sep-30''s completed session wearing a ''Just now'' timestamp, not live Oct-1 tape; the entry itself was honest (executed at the verified close price), but the trigger line was wrong by Rs 5.95. Invalidator corrected to ''close at/below Rs 261.70 → exit'' in current_state.json. Lesson: never set an invalidator off a single quote page''s prev-close field minutes after the open — triangulate the close against an independent dated source in the same run.

## Learnings
- 2026-10-01 07:06 ET: ONE-HUNDRED-SECOND RUN — post-close chain-preservation (~16:36 IST, ~1h06m after the Oct-1 NSE close; run 98 owned the decisive verdicts, runs 99–101 the guards), no trade. BTC 112th check: $83,880.01 (finnhub.io DIRECT open — GENUINE fresh tuple, not frozen: O 83,770.01, H 85,649.95, L 83,186, prev 83,770.01, +0.1313%; differs from the run-99 O 83,704.01 and run-100 O 83,872.68 tuples, so the stale-tick rule clears it) vs $83,382.01 entry (+0.60%) — flat band intact across 112 consecutive checks; BlackBull $83,782.00 (<1h crawl), swapzone $83,801.61, cryptocompass $83,776.93 (Oct-1 CoinGecko) all corroborate in-band; bestcryptochecker $84,150.30 / $83,355, nowprice $84,240, exchangerate.guru $84,242.18 all recycled (same prints 3h+ across runs) per the stale-tick rule. New spam variant logged: analyticsinsight.net''s ''crypto prices today'' template printed four mutually-contradictory BTC numbers ($77,468 / $76,347 / $78,970 / $79,800) against the $83–84k verified tape — these contradict every verified read AND each other, so the discard criterion is ''contradicts the verified consensus'' not just ''>5% off one read''. Fresh genuinely-dated news: Citi raised its 12-month BTC target to $113,000 from $82,000 (Reuters, Oct 1 — stronger crypto activity, supportive macro, resuming ETF inflows) — filed as constructive tone confirmation for the BTC thesis, NOT a trade trigger: an analyst target is a narrative, not a tape event, and with $0 crypto cash it has no executable surface anyway. Strategy''s 1,665 BTC Sep-28 buy = already-logged re-read. $0 crypto cash (100% BTC) = logged, not traded — selling flat-band BTC with no thesis would be churn. India CLOSED (reopens 11:45 PM ET; Rs 20,313.64 staged; sleeve MTM Rs 96,708.68, −3.29%); US CLOSED (opens 9:30 AM ET; $579.13 staged; NVDA/BA Sep-30 close invalidators HELD). Lesson: an analyst target raise on the name you already own at flat is the purest form of the ''tone confirmation'' bucket — it strengthens the thesis log without changing the decision, and naming why it doesn''t trade (narrative ≠ tape, zero cash) is what keeps the confirmation from becoming an excuse to force an entry. Next decisive events: US open 9:30 AM ET + India reopen 11:45 PM ET (Rs 20,313.64 deployment watchlist owned by the pre-open run).
- 2026-10-01 06:06 ET: NINETY-EIGHTH RUN - post-close decisive run, TRADE (SELL NLCINDIA, txn_011). Oct-1 close Rs 253.55 (finnhub direct open 3:36 PM IST, 6 min post-close: O 261.20, H 261.25, L 251.85, prev 261.70, -3.1143%; tickertape Rs 253.25 corroborates) - decisively below the ''close at/below Rs 261.70 -> exit (catalyst-day failed)'' invalidator named at entry, so the 80-share position sold at the close-area print for Rs 20,284.00, realized -Rs 652.00 (-3.11%). Catalyst facts were intact to the end (BESS LoA Rs 2.35 lakh/MW/month + Sep-29 board-approved 50:50 Nalco 1,080 MW JV, re-verified 16 times, zero negative news) - this was a tape-rejection exit, not a thesis-break exit, and the discipline worked exactly as designed: 97 runs of defense held the mid-session nerve (FLAG deepened -1.03% to -3.15% with zero mid-session action), and the pre-named trigger fired at the close. HILINFRA Rs 44.91 (+5.05% session, close-exit line Rs 42.75 untouched, HELD) - a +5% green first day validates the reasoned mid-fade entry thesis; BSE Rs 3,040.90 (-4.97% vs entry, held), POWERMECH Rs 2,482.20 (+0.44%, held), ARIS Rs 138.36 (-1.17%, held). BTC 108th check $83,183 (Morningstar/Dow Jones 05:06 ET; theagenttimes $83,375.18 corroborates) - flat band intact across 108 consecutive checks; $0 crypto cash = logged, not traded. Sleeve MTM Rs 96,708.68 (-3.29% vs initial; cash Rs 20,313.64 now staged for the next India session 11:45 PM ET; US opens 9:30 AM ET, $579.13 staged, NVDA/BA invalidators HELD Sep 30). Lesson: the decisive run''s whole job is verdict ownership - two pre-named triggers (NLCINDIA <= 261.70, HILINFRA <= 42.75) were each carried through ~10 runs as named owners, and the close print settled both in opposite directions without any mid-session override. A post-close finnhub direct open reads as the settled close when its day-range fields are continuous with the session tape - but verify against a second dated venue (tickertape) before executing, because the price is now the P&L, not a note.
